      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the apps are not time-sensitive and don\u0027t rely on the number of broadcast, I agree this should be fine.\nIf we are not sure about out assumption, it\u0027s better to guard by kill switch flag at least.\n\nAlso, I think it\u0027s better to have another parameter for this delay (or update the comment).\nI think the usage in this CL is different from this comment.\n```\n    /**\n     * When global alert quota is high, wait for this delay before processing each polling,\n     * and do not schedule further polls once there is already one queued.\n     * This avoids firing the global alert too often on devices with high transfer speeds and\n     * high quota.\n     */\n    private static final int DEFAULT_PERFORM_POLL_DELAY_MS \u003d 1000;\n```\n\nOther than that, LGTM but since I\u0027m not familiar with network stats code, I want to get opinion from @reminv@google.com.",
